$schema: https://usm.dev/schema/v1.json
$id: smith-gray/python-sdk
$type: service
$version: 1
$last_updated: "2026-09-22"
summary: |
  Python Agent SDK — a token-only client for agents building secret workflows (LangChain and LangGraph tools first). It exposes create_secret and resolve_for_tool, and by construction cannot return plaintext to the caller: it only ever returns capability tokens and folder paths.

$system: smith-gray/system
name: Python SDK
status: planned
type: api
runtime: python
port: 0
paths:
  - packages/sdk-python
depends_on:
  - cli

tech_stack:
  language: Python 3.11+
  packaging: pyproject.toml, published to PyPI
  agent_frameworks: LangChain and LangGraph tools first
  transport: local sidecar Unix socket

dev:
  command: "python -m pytest packages/sdk-python"
  url: ""
  env:
    SAFEKEYS_SOCKET: /run/safekeys/sidecar.sock

prod:
  url: ""
  region: ""
  deployment_ref: ""

testing:
  framework: pytest
  command: "pytest packages/sdk-python"
  coverage_target: "80%"

security:
  auth_method: Local sidecar socket
  secrets_ref: docs/help/security-model.md

modules:
  - name: client
    purpose: Sidecar socket client and token handling
    paths: [packages/sdk-python/safekeys]
  - name: tools
    purpose: LangChain / LangGraph tool definitions (create_secret, resolve_for_tool)
    paths: [packages/sdk-python/safekeys/tools]

risks:
  - "A developer could bypass the SDK and handle plaintext directly; the SDK's value is that its API surface makes the safe path the easy path."

future:
  - "TypeScript SDK with an identical API surface."
  - "OpenAI Agents SDK adapter built on the same tools."

decisions:
  - id: token-only-api
    decision: The SDK API accepts and returns only tokens and folder paths — never plaintext values.
    rationale: Making plaintext unrepresentable in the type surface means an agent using the SDK cannot accidentally route a value through model context.
    status: accepted
